    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Funciones\n",
        "\n",
        "- `omega_sage(e)`: arma y² − $ \\prod (x − eᵢ) $, le pide a Sage la superficie y su matriz de periodos. Esa Ω está en la base que escoge Sage.\n",
        "- `theta_sorted(Ω)`: las 10 theta constantes pares, en valor absoluto, divididas por la mayor y ordenadas. Un cambio de base no las afecta**."
      ],
      "id": "c5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c6"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import itertools\n",
        "\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from sage.all__sagemath_schemes import *\n",
        "from sage.schemes.riemann_surfaces.riemann_surface import RiemannSurface\n",
        "\n",
        "R = PolynomialRing(QQ, \"x,y\")\n",
        "x, y = R.gens()\n",
        "\n",
        "GRIS = \"#52514e\"\n",
        "C1, C2, C3 = \"#2a78d6\", \"#eb6834\", \"#1baf7a\"\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def omega_sage(e, prec=53):\n",
        "    ee = [QQ(round(float(v) * 10**12)) / 10**12 for v in e]\n",
        "    S = RiemannSurface(y**2 - prod(x - v for v in ee), prec=prec)\n",
        "    M = S.riemann_matrix()\n",
        "    return np.array([[complex(M[i, j]) for j in range(2)] for i in range(2)])\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def even_characteristics():\n",
        "    pares = []\n",
        "    for a in itertools.product([0, 1], repeat=2):\n",
        "        for b in itertools.product([0, 1], repeat=2):\n",
        "            if np.dot(a, b) % 2 == 0:\n",
        "                pares.append((np.array(a), np.array(b)))\n",
        "    return pares\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def theta_sorted(Om, N=5):\n",
        "    vals = []\n",
        "    rango = range(-N, N + 1)\n",
        "    for a, b in even_characteristics():\n",
        "        s = 0\n",
        "        for n1 in rango:\n",
        "            for n2 in rango:\n",
        "                v = np.array([n1, n2]) + a / 2\n",
        "                s += np.exp(1j * np.pi * (v @ Om @ v) + 1j * np.pi * (v @ b))\n",
        "        vals.append(abs(s))\n",
        "    vals = np.array(vals)\n",
        "    return np.sort(vals / vals.max())\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def limpiar(ax):\n",
        "    for lado in [\"top\", \"right\"]:\n",
        "        ax.spines[lado].set_visible(False)\n",
        "    ax.tick_params(colors=GRIS)\n",
        "    ax.grid(axis=\"y\", color=\"#e8e7e3\", lw=0.8)\n"
      ],
      "id": "c6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Experimento: probar un camino continuo de superficies\n",
        "\n",
        "Se mueven los puntos de ramificación en línea recta de e = (0, .15, .40, .80, 1, 2) a e = (0, .45, .62, .90, 1, 2) en 40 pasos. Ω debería cambiar poco a poco.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para cada superficie se revisa la validez y se cuenta un salto cuando alguna entrada de Ω cambia más de 0.1 entre pasos seguidos."
      ],
      "id": "c7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c8",
        "outputId": "aa82f22b-c370-46ca-ec9e-26655b52bf25"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "max error de simetria: 3.7756666593398424e-15\n",
            "min autovalor de Im Omega: 0.27673934026405345\n",
            "saltos en Omega: 20 de 39 pasos\n",
            "cambio max de las theta ordenadas, pasos sin salto: 0.00719428606094219\n",
            "cambio max de las theta ordenadas, pasos con salto: 0.004763934591003327\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "eA = np.array([0, 0.15, 0.40, 0.80, 1, 2])\n",
        "eB = np.array([0, 0.45, 0.62, 0.90, 1, 2])\n",
        "s_vals = np.linspace(0, 1, 40)\n",
        "\n",
        "Om_camino = []\n",
        "q_camino = []\n",
        "for s in s_vals:\n",
        "    Om = omega_sage((1 - s) * eA + s * eB)\n",
        "    Om_camino.append(Om)\n",
        "    q_camino.append(theta_sorted(Om))\n",
        "Om_camino = np.array(Om_camino)\n",
        "q_camino = np.array(q_camino)\n",
        "\n",
        "sym = [np.linalg.norm(Om - Om.T) for Om in Om_camino]\n",
        "min_eig = [np.linalg.eigvalsh(Om.imag).min() for Om in Om_camino]\n",
        "print(\"max error de simetria:\", max(sym))\n",
        "print(\"min autovalor de Im Omega:\", min(min_eig))\n",
        "\n",
        "dOm = np.abs(np.diff(Om_camino, axis=0)).max(axis=(1, 2))\n",
        "dq = np.abs(np.diff(q_camino, axis=0)).max(axis=1)\n",
        "salto = dOm > 0.1\n",
        "print(\"saltos en Omega:\", salto.sum(), \"de\", len(dOm), \"pasos\")\n",
        "print(\"cambio max de las theta ordenadas, pasos sin salto:\", dq[~salto].max())\n",
        "print(\"cambio max de las theta ordenadas, pasos con salto:\", dq[salto].max())\n"
      ],
      "id": "c8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c9"
      },
      "source": [
        "todas las Ω pasan los controles de validez. La huella cambia lo mismo en los pasos con salto que en los normales; las superficies no saltan, lo que salta es la base de lazos que escoge Sage."
      ],
      "id": "c9"
    },
